# text = Jane , you don't like my narrative ; you look almost sick -- shall I defer the rest to another day No , sir , finish it now ; I pity you -- I do earnestly pity you Pity , Jane , from some people is a noxious and insulting sort of tribute , which one is justified in hurling back in the teeth of those who offer it ; but that is the sort of pity native to callous , selfish hearts ; it is a hybrid , egotistical pain at hearing of woes , crossed with ignorant contempt for those who have endured them .
